dialect protocol
protocol stdio.pdf.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.pdf.op
start op

# P2-FG3: `protocol::OpBinary::encode_op`/`decode_op` for `stdio.pdf` (1.4) are hand-rolled
# (../../🦀️component.rs's `OpCodecs` region) since ticket 26/08/23/END-TO-END-TESTING-REFACTOR
# gave this standard a real page tree — the derive path's generic `os_pack::encode_record_body`
# wire (a varint-prefixed string-symbol table plus a self-describing per-field-id TAG stream) is
# framework-generic and, as this dialect stands today, structurally irreducible here; a hand-rolled
# frame is not.
#
# Layout, byte for byte as `encode_op` writes it: a fixed `format` byte
# (`store::pack_rt::OP_BINARY_FORMAT`), then the variant tag as a single byte in declaration order
# (`NoMutation`=0, `SetSnapshot`=1), then the variant's own payload. `NoMutation` has none;
# `SetSnapshot` carries `enc_snapshot_bin` — a length-prefixed schema string, a varint page count,
# and per page two little-endian `f64`s plus a length-prefixed text. The payload is genuinely
# structured binary, never the text form's bytes.
#
# `header fixed 2` + `chain payload bytes` is the honest shape: `format` and `tag` are individually
# walked and validated; the variant payload past them is a length-driven chain this dialect has no
# per-variant dispatch primitive for.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8
chain payload bytes
